Thanks — I can help with this. A couple quick clarifying points before I draft or send anything:

- Your note says “My last A1C was 320.” A1C is normally reported as a percent (e.g., 6.5%) and a value of 320 would be more like a blood glucose in mg/dL. Can you confirm whether you meant A1C percent or a glucose number?
- Do you want me to draft an email to your PCP (Dr. Amy Foster) now, save it as a draft, or send it? If sending, please confirm the email address to use (or tell me to use the one on file).

Below are two things I can do immediately: (1) suggested questions to bring up with your PCP about atrial fibrillation management and orthopedic referral; and (2) a ready-to-use email template to Dr. Foster that I can send or save as a draft if you want.

1) Suggested questions to ask your PCP (short, high-priority)
- Atrial fibrillation (AFib)
  - Do I need anticoagulation based on my stroke risk (CHA2DS2-VASc score)? If yes, what medication do you recommend and why?
  - Should I be referred to cardiology or an electrophysiologist for AFib management?
  - Do I need an ECG, ambulatory monitoring (Holter/patch), or echocardiogram before the visit?
  - What symptoms should prompt urgent evaluation (palpitations, dizziness, syncope, worsening shortness of breath)?
  - Are any of my current meds (lisinopril, atorvastatin, omeprazole) relevant to AFib treatment choices or interactions?
- Orthopedics / back pain
  - Given my age and history, do you recommend a referral to Northwest Orthopedics now?
  - Would you want imaging first (X-ray, MRI), or try more conservative measures (PT, injections)?
  - Do I need assessment for fall risk or bone health (DEXA scan, vitamin D, calcium)?
- Preparation for annual physical / tests
  - Which labs or screening tests should be done beforehand? (A1C, lipid panel, CMP, CBC, TSH, urine, ECG, others)
  - Any medication adjustments or monitoring you want me to do before the appointment?

2) Email template to Dr. Amy Foster (ready to send or save as draft)
Subject: Questions before annual physical — AFib management and possible ortho referral

Body:
Hello Dr. Foster —

I’m preparing for my annual physical and have two main concerns I’d like to address:

1) Atrial fibrillation management — I would like your advice about stroke prevention and whether I should be on anticoagulation given my age and medical history. Also, should I be referred to cardiology/electrophysiology or get any pre-visit tests (ECG, Holter, echo)?

2) Chronic back pain — I’m wondering if a referral to Northwest Orthopedics is appropriate now, or if you’d prefer imaging or conservative treatments first. Also, should I be assessed for bone health (DEXA) or fall risk?

My current medications: omeprazole 20 mg daily, lisinopril 20 mg daily, atorvastatin 40 mg daily. (Please confirm if you have the same med list on file.)

My last reported A1C in my notes reads “320” — I believe that may be an error; could you check the correct A1C or tell me which labs I should have done before the visit?

Please let me know:
- Whether you recommend any specific tests before the appointment
- If you think a referral to cardiology or orthopedics is needed now
- Any other instructions or information I should bring

Thank you,
[Your Full Name]
DOB: [mm/dd/yyyy]
Preferred phone: [your phone number]

---

