Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
Yes — I can help. Below are focused questions and actions you can use for your PCP visit (or send to Dr. Amy Foster). I also flagged one likely error you should confirm.

Quick check
- Your note says “last A1C was 320” — that’s almost certainly a typo (A1C is normally reported as a percent, e.g., 6.4%). Can you confirm the actual A1C or blood glucose value before I include it in any message?

Questions to ask about atrial fibrillation (or if you’re worried about AF)
- Symptoms & history
  - Have you seen any palpitations, skipped beats, dizziness, shortness of breath, chest pain, or fainting? If yes, how often and how long?
  - Should I keep a symptom log (time/date/duration/activity) or use a smartphone ECG app?
- Diagnostic testing
  - Can we get a 12‑lead ECG today? If ECG is normal but I have symptoms, should I have a Holter monitor (24–48 hr) or an event monitor (longer) or an implantable loop recorder?
  - Should I get an echocardiogram to check cardiac structure/function?
- Stroke risk and anticoagulation
  - What is my estimated stroke risk (CHA2DS2‑VASc) and do you recommend anticoagulation?
  - If anticoagulation is recommended, what are the pros/cons of a DOAC vs warfarin for me? Any kidney‑function checks needed first?
