I can help with both: (A) a focused list of questions to take to your PCP about atrial fibrillation and whether you need an orthopedics referral, and (B) a ready-to-send/draft email to Dr. Amy Foster summarizing your concerns. Before I create/send the email, two quick clarifying points:

- Can you confirm your current medications and doses? Your memory note looks a bit mixed-up (omeprazole is for reflux, lisinopril for blood pressure, atorvastatin for cholesterol). Please list the meds you’re actually taking and doses.
- Do you already have a diagnosis of atrial fibrillation, or are you asking about risk/management because of symptoms or screening results?

If that’s correct, here are suggested questions and a draft email you can use.

Suggested questions to ask Dr. Amy Foster about atrial fibrillation (AF) management
- Do I have AF (or is there concern for it)? If so, what type (paroxysmal, persistent, permanent)?
- Do I need diagnostic testing before my visit? (ECG, 24–48h Holter, event monitor, echocardiogram)
- Based on my age, comorbidities, and meds, do I need anticoagulation to reduce stroke risk? If so, what agent do you recommend and why?
- If anticoagulation is recommended, how will we monitor bleeding risk and interactions with my current meds?
- Should we consider rate control or rhythm control strategies (medications vs cardiology referral for ablation)?
- Do you recommend a cardiology or electrophysiology referral now, or only if symptoms/worsening tests occur?
- Are any of my current medications (or OTC supplements) that I take now problematic if I start anticoagulation or AF meds?
- Any lifestyle changes or symptom monitoring you want me to do before the appointment (BP log, pulse checks, symptom diary)?
- Given my upcoming travel to Italy, any precautions or medication adjustments I should plan for?

Suggested questions about your back pain and possible referral to orthopedics (Northwest Orthopedics)
- Based on my age and history, do you recommend imaging (X-ray, MRI) before referring to orthopedics?
- Have I tried appropriate conservative measures (physical therapy, targeted injections, medication optimization)? If not, can you refer or prescribe?
- Are there “red flags” you’re concerned about that would make urgent referral necessary (neurologic deficits, major function loss)?
- Would you recommend referral to Northwest Orthopedics now, or trial conservative treatment first? If you recommend them, can you send a referral and include any imaging or notes?
- Should I be evaluated for bone density or fall-risk given my age and anemia/other conditions?

Ready-to-send/draft email to Dr. Amy Foster
