I can help with this — would you like me to draft or send an email to your PCP (Dr. Amy Foster) right now, or just help you prepare questions for your appointment? Below I’ve prepared a concise email you can send and a short list of focused questions to bring up about atrial fibrillation management and an orthopedics referral.

Suggested subject
- Questions about atrial fibrillation management and possible ortho referral

Suggested email body
Hi Dr. Foster — I hope you’re well. Ahead of my annual physical I wanted to ask about two things:

1) Atrial fibrillation / stroke prevention — I have a history of hypertension and other health concerns (see meds below). I’m worried about AFib management and whether I need monitoring or anticoagulation. Could you advise whether I need any testing (ECG/Holter/echo), a cardiology referral, or starting anticoagulation? If anticoagulation is appropriate, what options do you recommend given my current meds?

2) Back pain / orthopedics referral — I’ve had ongoing back pain and want to know whether you recommend a referral to Northwest Orthopedics for evaluation, imaging, or conservative treatment. Given my age and risk factors, should I get imaging (X-ray/MRI) or a DEXA scan first?

Quick medical summary:
- Age: 55
- Conditions: hypertension, anemia, history of back pain
- Current meds: omeprazole 20 mg daily, lisinopril 20 mg, atorvastatin 40 mg
- Recent labs: (please confirm — my last A1C listed as 320 in my notes; that may be an error)

Would you prefer a brief phone/telemed visit to discuss or should I schedule an in‑person appointment? Thanks — I appreciate your guidance.

[Your name / preferred contact info]

Suggested questions to bring up or include in the email
- Do I currently have atrial fibrillation or is it suspected? If so, what is my stroke risk and does that warrant anticoagulation?
- Which anticoagulation options are best for me (warfarin vs DOAC)? Any drug interactions with my current meds (omeprazole, lisinopril, atorvastatin)?
- Do I need an ECG, echocardiogram, Holter monitor, or cardiology referral?
- For back pain: should I get imaging first (X-ray vs MRI) or try further conservative care (PT, injections) before a referral?
- Given my age and risk profile, should I have a DEXA scan or other tests related to bone health?
- Any lab updates or vaccinations needed before travel to Italy next month?

Next steps — what would you like me to do?
- I can send this email to Dr. Amy Foster for you now (I can look up her contact in your inbox).
- I can save it as a draft for you to review/edit.
- I can just keep helping you refine the questions or checklist for the appointment.

One quick clarification: your memory note lists “last A1C was 320” — did you mean 3.20% (unlikely) or 320 mg/dL for a glucose reading? Please confirm the correct lab value so I can include accurate info in the message.

